From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:38:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a takeover's re-attach burst builds each
 session's banner inventory sections once per profile

When the hub's socket moves to the gateway that took over (gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn closes the kept socket with 1012 once the next gateway is ready), the hub re-attaches every chat it watches, one after the other: session.events.since, session.resume and config.set each. Every session.resume built the session's banner inventory again (snapshot_info: the git branch and project of its folder, the tool snapshot of its policy, the availability of its toolsets, the skills, the MCP servers, the CLI notices), though the chats of one profile share those sections. On a CPU-starved gateway (0.5 CPU) that was most of each resume (0.1 to 0.4 s): a streaming reply that the hub re-attached late paused for seconds (4.1 to 4.5 s with it last of eight chats), and the API turns running at that moment waited for the CPU (up to 2 s over their median).

The profile-wide sections are now reused for INVENTORY_REUSE_S (10 s) once built, keyed by what each depends on (the folder, the frozen policy without the session's own secret reference, the toolset list) and per profile (session_local_inventory._section, under reused_session_inventory). The sections only a session's own agent knows (its tools, provider, system prompt, context length) are read each time. Callers of one key at once wait for the one build; each gets its own copy. session.info, which a client sends to see the inventory of now, builds every section anew.
